/* Two columns and three rows: the checkout's own heading, who is standing on
   it, what was left here — and what this checkout would land, up beside the
   heading and spanning down past the figures. Every one of them is `auto` or
   content-sized, so a band with one quiet agent is a strip and a band with five
   is tall. The mockup gave them all the same generous rhythm, and that was most
   of what the direction cost in height against a page that packs them. */
.band{display:grid;gap:0 14px;padding:1px 0 3px;align-items:start;
 grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;
 grid-template-areas:"wt gate" "floor gate" "left left"}
/* The worktree path, as this strip's own heading. It used to stand in a narrow
   column down the left, where a real path broke across four lines mid-word and
   then SET the band's height. One line now, and cut on the LEFT, because a
   checkout is told apart by its tail: `…/.claude/worktrees/support-tickets`
   identifies it where `~/work/shopfront/shopfr…` does not. The cut is CSS
   and never string surgery — the whole path stays in the element, so it selects
   and copies whole, and it is in the title as well. */
.wt{grid-area:wt;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:9px;min-width:0;
