/* Beside the figure there is exactly as much room as the figure is TALL, and the
   ground line is drawn across the bottom of it. So that room is a band with a
   floor and not the top of a column that runs on: anything laid out in it past
   the figure's legs is laid out ON the line, and comes out struck through — which
   is what a declared task did, out to the right edge of the strip.
   The band carries who this agent is and what it SAID: its name, its chips, and
   its speech bubble, which belongs up here anyway because its tail points at the
   figure. What the bus DERIVED begins below the line, in the figure's own column
   — what it last did, the work it declared, the subagents standing under it, how
   long it has been quiet. That is not a new shape. It is the shape an agent with
   a bubble already had, because a name and a one-line bubble fill the band almost
   exactly; and below the ground in the figure's column is where the subagent tree
   already hangs, on a spine that starts at the parent's feet and carries the
   ground's own colour down. What was wrong is that the band was only ever filled
   by a bubble, so an agent that had said nothing let its next line slide up into
   the ground line's own row, and which line landed there was luck.
   `--say` is the band's height and `.info`'s offset is the rest of the figure, so
   the two cannot drift apart: the band's floor IS the figure's feet. A bubble with
   more in it than the band holds still crosses the line — but a bubble is opaque
   and stands in front of it, which reads as an object on the ground rather than as
   a struck-out sentence. */
