/* What it last ACTUALLY did, under what it said it was doing. Derived from the
   tool calls the hooks already see, so it costs the agents nothing to say and
   cannot be got wrong on purpose — and it is deliberately not in the speech
   bubble above it, because that one is the agent talking and this one is the
   bus watching. Ten pixels in, so its first character sits under the bubble's
   rather than ten to the left of it: what was said and what was done are a pair
   and have to read as one.
   ONE LINE, and cut — the same treatment the worktree path above it gets, and
   for the same reason. Wrapped, this line was three lines for one agent and one
   for its neighbour, and since it is the LAST thing in a cell that variance went
   straight into how far each figure's content hung below the strip they are all
   standing on. Four parts, and only one of them can be cut: the verb, the tool's
   target, where that target is when it is not in this checkout, and how long
   ago. The clock reading is why the line must never be cut from the right —
   "editing basket.ts, 40m ago" and "editing basket.ts, 2s ago" are different
   facts and the cut may not be allowed to eat the difference.
   Which END of the target goes is a property of what the target IS. A command is
   identified by its head — `pnpm --filter …` says what it is and the flags after
   it do not — so it keeps its head. A path is identified by its tail, exactly as
   a worktree path is, so it keeps its filename and loses its directories. The
   cut is CSS and never string surgery: the whole thing stays in the element, so
   it selects and copies whole, and it is in the title as well. */
