/* ---- a session's subagents, as a tree under it -------------------------- */
/* A subagent is a party in its own right in this system: it holds locks under
   its own `agent_id`, it contends with its siblings, it can take work, and the
   whole `same_party` machinery exists for it. It used to be a half-size figure
   at its parent's feet plus a chip counting them, carrying no branch, no
   checkout and no work — so it read as decoration, and a subagent holding the
   simulator was a dot. Drawn under its parent and indented, the parent-child
   relation is the first thing read.
   The rows are SHORT, and not padded to look equal: unread, commits past the
   trunk and files written are all counted per session, so they belong to the
   parent and repeating them here would be inventing facts about the child. */
/* The spine starts at the parent's FEET, which is the one position on this row
   that is known by construction: the ground line is `--fh` from the top of the
   row, and everything below it depends on how much this agent had to say. It
   runs down the empty column under the figure to the bottom of the row, where
   the first child picks it up — and it is the ground's own colour, because that
   is what it is carrying down. An agent with nothing to say is exactly `--fh`
   tall, so the segment is then zero high and nothing is drawn. */
